{"ts": 1791255356.0461152, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Nice\u2014this suggests the eval idea is still a bit shaky, so let\u2019s do a focused pass.\n\nPlease open/read the Week 3 evaluation reading again, especially the parts on pass@k vs pass^k and proxy vs direct measures. Then send me:\n1) a one-sentence definition of pass^k,\n2) the minimum number of seeds you need for the build,\n3) one sentence explaining why pass^k is the right metric here.\n\nIf you\u2019re unsure, I\u2019ll correct it and help you turn it into the writeup text.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=13 messages 2m", "t": 15, "activity": [{"t": 13, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.3847194656129005, "pass_k": 0.3592640943928733}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8330104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.32481971324228814, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255357.814273, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is:\n\npass^k means **all k runs succeed**.\n\nFor your build, you should report **pass^k over at least 3 seeds**. So if you run 3 seeds, pass^k is 1 only if all 3 seeds succeed; otherwise it\u2019s 0.\n\nWhy this metric: the build is about **reliability**, not just whether you get lucky once. That\u2019s why pass^k fits better than pass@k.\n\nYou can paste this into your writeup:\n\u201cpass^k measures the fraction of seeds for which the agent succeeds on every run; unlike pass@k, which only asks whether at least one run succeeds, pass^k reflects deployment reliability. We report pass^k over 3 seeds.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: makes sense. what next?\n[activity] t=15 messages 1m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 15, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.3847194656129005, "pass_k": 0.36460723945875767}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8330104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.40481971324228816, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255359.023191, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Next, let\u2019s make your environment definition precise and writeable.\n\nPlease draft 3 bullets:\n1) State: what information fully describes the task situation?\n2) Observations: what does the agent actually see each step?\n3) Actions: what can the agent choose to do?\n\nThen send me your draft and I\u2019ll tighten it up into build-ready wording. If you already have a task in mind, include it too (e.g. quiz agent, study assistant, etc.).", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: makes sense. what next?\n[activity] t=16 messages 2m", "t": 18, "activity": [{"t": 16, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.4631248080165907, "pass_k": 0.36460723945875767}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8330104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.4248197132422882, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255360.24252, "type": "step", "step": 27, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Next step: let\u2019s lock down your environment definition so the writeup is complete.\n\nReply with a rough draft in this format:\n- **State:** ...\n- **Observations:** ...\n- **Actions:** ...\n- **Dynamics / transitions:** ...\n- **What counts as success:** ...\n\nIf you want, I can turn your draft into a polished paragraph after you send it.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\nStudent: I don't really get pomdp yet\n[activity] t=18 messages 2m", "t": 20, "activity": [{"t": 18, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.5316466258334558, "pass_k": 0.36460723945875767}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8330104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.4448197132422882, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255361.99346, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Absolutely \u2014 POMDP just means the agent **doesn\u2019t get to see the whole state**.\n\nThink of it like this:\n- **State** = the full truth of the world\n- **Observation** = only the part the agent can see\n- **Belief** = the agent\u2019s best guess about the hidden state\n\nSo if the student/agent can\u2019t directly observe everything important, it\u2019s a POMDP.\n\nFor your build, the practical takeaway is:\n- your environment may have hidden variables\n- the agent may need to act with incomplete information\n- sometimes **gathering more information is itself an action** and can have a cost\n\nShort version you can use in notes:\n\u201cPOMDPs are environments where the agent cannot observe the full state, so it must act from partial observations and maintain a belief about what the hidden state might be.\u201d\n\nIf you want, I can next help you connect this directly to your specific build environment.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\n[activity] t=20 messages 4m", "t": 24, "activity": [{"t": 20, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.609017780945101, "pass_k": 0.36460723945875767}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8330104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.4448197132422882, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": []}}
